{
  "id": "COMPOUND:43279 - PROTEIN:6147",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a direct relationship between Spirostan-3,27-diol, (3alpha)- and Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, mediated through the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This pathway is supported by multiple independent connections, all of which indicate that Spirostan-3,27-diol, (3alpha)- acts as a target for various compounds that ultimately interact with the SDR family member. The shared involvement of the 26S proteasome subunit in these relationships implies a potential role in cellular processes such as protein degradation or signaling, which could be a common mechanism across the different targets. The consistent presence of the SDR family member as a target in multiple pathways suggests that it may be a key player in the metabolic or enzymatic processes influenced by Spirostan-3,27-diol, (3alpha)-. The evidence does not provide direct evidence of the mechanism by which Spirostan-3,27-diol, (3alpha)- interacts with the SDR family member, but the presence of multiple intermediaries and the shared regulatory subunit supports a plausible, indirect interaction pathway.",
